@title bit Generations - Dotstream (Japan)
@file Bit Generations Dotstream (J).gba
@game BVCJ
@chip SRAM
@frozen dingbat-bios,mgba,nba

# Health warning, A, the dotstream logo, START, campaign, sonic GP class 1,
# drawing-1, the line select: the race. The player's line (orange) holds UP
# from f2206 and scrapes along the top wall; on the second lap a block there
# ends it ("retire", f8806). The result, A: total GP points, A: the race
# select moves on to drawing-2, and the GP standings are in SRAM (26 bytes,
# twice). [load]: warning, logo (the first START comes too early on every
# emulator and is not taken), campaign, sonic GP: drawing-2, GP rank 6.
# All three emulators draw every fade between screens differently (15-frame
# runs from f145 on: dingbat-bios, mgba and the second reference each a
# shade apart), so none is the odd one out. From f2010 the second reference
# runs its own race: the computer lines take other paths, its race clock
# ends 4 hundredths off, and its result and GP points (so its save) differ.
# dingbat-bios and mgba hash alike on every race frame.

[new]
wait 300
checkpoint warning window=30
press A
wait 300
wait 120
checkpoint logo window=30
press START
wait 120
checkpoint main_menu window=30
press A
wait 120
checkpoint gp_select window=30
press A
wait 150
checkpoint race_select window=30
press A
wait 200
press A
wait 200
checkpoint race_start window=30
wait 300
hold UP
wait 300
wait 300
wait 300
wait 240
checkpoint racing window=30
wait 600
wait 600
wait 1200
wait 1200
wait 1740
checkpoint retire window=30
release
wait 300
press A
wait 200
press A
wait 200
checkpoint next_race window=30
[load]
wait 300
press A
wait 300
wait 120
press START
wait 120
checkpoint continue_logo window=30
press START
wait 120
press A
wait 120
press A
wait 150
checkpoint race2_select window=30
press A
wait 200
checkpoint gp_rank window=30
